  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 10 files that trace the exception path end to end:\n\n**Netty (origin \u2192 propagation \u2192 unhandled tail):**\n1. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/nio/AbstractNioByteChannel.java` \u2014 `NioByteUnsafe.handleReadException` is where a socket-level `IOException` (e.g. connection reset) is caught during `read()` and turned into `pipeline.fireExceptionCaught(cause)`.\n2. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/AbstractChannelHandlerContext.java` \u2014 `invokeExceptionCaught` propagates the exception inbound through the pipeline.\n3. `transport/src/main/java/io/netty/channel/DefaultChannelPipeline.java` \u2014 `onUnhandledInboundException` is the tail behavior when no handler consumes the exception (just logs a warning by default).\n4. `handler/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/ssl/SslHandler.java` \u2014 explicitly swallows \"connection reset by peer\"/\"broken pipe\" as a harmless SSL-layer event, another point where the original signal can be downgraded before reaching the app.\n\n**Spring (reactor-netty bridge \u2192 WebFlux terminal handling):**\n5. `spring-web/.../http/server/reactive/ReactorHttpHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 adapts reactor-netty's `HttpServerRequest`/`HttpServerResponse` BiFunction into Spring's `HttpHandler` contract; errors only get a trace-level log (`doOnError`) with no context enrichment.\n6. `spring-web/.../web/server/adapter/HttpWebHandlerAdapter.java` \u2014 **the key file**: `handleUnresolvedError`/`isDisconnectedClientError` is where a generic `Throwable` becomes either a swallowed \"client went away\" (via brittle substring matching on `\"broken pipe\"`/`\"connection reset by peer\"` in the message) or a logged-but-context-stripped 500.\n7. `spring-web/.../http/server/reactive/HttpHandler.java` \u2014 the interface contract (`Mono<Void> handle(request, response)`) that erases everything but a reactive error signal; no channel/pipeline metadata crosses this boundary.\n8. `spring-web/.../web/server/WebExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 the exchange-level exception handler SPI.\n9. `spring-web/.../web/server/handler/ExceptionHandlingWebHandler.java` \u2014 chains `WebExceptionHandler`s.\n10. `spring-web/.../web/server/handler/ResponseStatusExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 how known Spring exceptions get typed responses (contrast with the generic path Netty-originated errors take).",
